{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Like the practice of the land of Egypt and like the practice of the land of Canaan.</b> Rabbi Yosi HaGelili says: since the practice of the land of Egypt is weighed against the practice of the land of Canaan, and the practice of the land of Canaan against the practice of the land of Egypt — why did the Canaanites merit to dwell in their land forty-seven years more? As it is written: ״And Hebron was built seven years before Zoan of Egypt.״ Rather, in the merit that they buried Abraham our father in the Cave of Machpelah, they merited. And this passage is juxtaposed here because above, the matter of the goats was mentioned, which they were occupied with at Passover in Egypt."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:08.492781268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}